'
' States of the worker thread as published in sysctl qnx.module.score_dlt.state.
' Values: src/qnx/qnx_module_stats.h (DLT_STATE_*). Transitions: src/qnx/iosock_module.c.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg -o diagrams worker_state.puml   (from qnx_iosock_dlt/doc, or the PlantUML extension of the editor)

@startuml worker_state
title Worker state (sysctl qnx.module.score_dlt.state)

[*] --> IDLE : module loaded
IDLE : 0
RUNNING : 1
FINISHED : 2
FAILED : 3

IDLE --> RUNNING : ring (ring input), socket and session are ready
IDLE --> FAILED : ring, socket or session setup failed
RUNNING --> FINISHED : stop requested, or (synthetic input)\nall records sent
FINISHED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note right of FINISHED
  The ring variant only reaches FINISHED on a stop
  request, which needs MOD_UNLOAD and is therefore
  not reachable today: it stays in RUNNING.
end note
@enduml
